annotation.description:
Marks the following class, function, or variable/property declaration as eligible for configured export-time obfuscation passes without changing its access rules. Right now, name obfuscation is the only implemented obfuscation pass, so this annotation currently affects exported names only. Future obfuscation passes may also use it for other transformations such as control-flow obfuscation or string encryption. When [code]wgodot/export/obfuscate_names[/code] is enabled, exported GDScript rewrites this declaration and analyzed usages to the same obfuscated name. On a class, all eligible members in that class are obfuscated unless their declarations use [annotation @no_mangle]. On a global [code]class_name[/code], the exported global class name and exported global script class cache entry are also rewritten. This is intentionally explicit and does not rewrite string-reflection calls such as [code]get("member_name")[/code], or resource/string references to global class names; use [annotation @no_mangle] when a dynamically accessed member or class must keep its original name. This annotation can be combined with [annotation @no_mangle]; in that case, [annotation @no_mangle] wins and the declaration keeps its original name. [codeblock] @obfuscate class_name PlayerAccount
@obfuscate var public_cache: Dictionary
@obfuscate func rebuild_cache() -> void: pass [/codeblock]

Marks a script or class as participating in wgodot partial-script declarations. The optional [param path] argument can identify the source fragment or companion script path used by tooling.
This annotation is currently recognized by the parser so projects and tools can use the marker without producing an unknown annotation error.
[codeblock]
@partial
class_name PlayerController

@partial("res://player/player_controller_input.gd")
class InputPart:
	pass
[/codeblock]

Marks the following class-level member as private to the current class.
Private members cannot be accessed from outside the class that declares them. Private fields, properties, and functions are also eligible for export-time name obfuscation when wgodot name obfuscation is enabled. Combine this annotation with [annotation @no_mangle] to keep the private access rule while opting that declaration out of export-time name obfuscation. This annotation can be used on nested classes, constants, functions, signals, and variables, and cannot be combined with [annotation @protected].
[codeblock]
@private
var inventory_cache: Dictionary

@private
func rebuild_cache() -> void:
	pass
[/codeblock]

Marks the following class-level member as protected.
Protected members can be accessed from the class that declares them and from inherited classes, but not from unrelated classes. This annotation can be used on nested classes, constants, functions, signals, and variables, and cannot be combined with [annotation @private].
[codeblock]
@protected
var health: int

@protected
func apply_damage(amount: int) -> void:
	pass
[/codeblock]

Marks the following variable as assignable only during initialization.
Local variables marked [annotation @readonly] must be assigned where they are declared. Class fields marked [annotation @readonly] can be assigned where they are declared or inside the class initializer, but cannot be reassigned later.
[codeblock]
@readonly
var id := 0

func example() -> void:
	@readonly
	var label := "ready"
[/codeblock]
